## fish-shell

The `cli-completions-data-fish` crate embeds a snapshot of completion
data extracted from [fish-shell](https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell).
fish-shell is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version
2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)**.

- Copyright © 2005–2009 Axel Liljencrantz
- Copyright © 2009– fish-shell contributors

The full text of the GPL-2.0 is reproduced in the license texts at the end of
this file, under `cli-completions-data-fish`. fish-shell's own COPYING notice,
kept with the data crate as `crates/cli-completions-data-fish/LICENSE-fish`,
reads:

```
Fish is a smart and user-friendly command line shell.

Copyright (C) 2005-2009 Axel Liljencrantz
Copyright (C) 2009- fish-shell contributors

fish is free software.

Most of fish is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2, and
you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU GPL as
published by the Free Software Foundation.

fish also includes software licensed under the Python Software Foundation License version 2, the MIT
license, and the GNU Library General Public License version 2.

Full licensing information is contained in doc_src/license.rst.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT
ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the GNU General Public License for
more details.
```

Source for fish-shell is publicly available at the upstream URL above.
The exact snapshot commit and date are recorded in
`crates/cli-completions-data-fish/data/fish-snapshot.toml` (when the
snapshot is vendored locally).

Because the compiled VSIX includes data derived from fish-shell, the
combined work is itself distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later. See
[LICENSE.md](LICENSE.md), and §11 "License: GPL-2 Compatibility" of RFC 005 —
[`docs/rfc/_archive/005-cli-completions-crate.md`](https://github.com/xuwaters/vscode-extensions/blob/main/docs/rfc/_archive/005-cli-completions-crate.md#11-license-gpl-2-compatibility)
in this repository — for the design rationale.

This section is written by hand, in `crates/makefile-analyzer/about.hbs`:
cargo-about reports the data crate's licence, below, but cannot know where its
data came from or whose it is.

## Rust dependencies

`wasm/makefile_analyzer_bg.wasm` statically links the crates listed here.
Crates from this repository are among them, and their holder is Wei Xu; those
without a license file of their own show the license template's placeholder
copyright line. They are MIT, except `cli-completions-data-fish`, which is
GPL-2.0-or-later because of the data it carries.

